    "- Administrative (regulatory) law: rules issued by government agencies (for example health or financial regulators); enforced through fines and sanctions.",
    "- Other systems: common law (precedent), civil/code law, religious and customary law. Know the branch from the scenario: prison = criminal, money between parties = civil, agency rules = administrative.",
    "## Key US laws",
    "- Computer Fraud and Abuse Act (CFAA): unauthorized access to federal interest computers.",
