    "- Federal Information Security Management Act (FISMA, modernized 2014): federal agencies must run information security programs (NIST guidance).",
    "- HIPAA (with HITECH): privacy and security of protected health information (PHI) for covered entities and business associates; HITECH adds breach notification and requires business associate agreements.",
    "- GLBA: privacy of financial information held by financial institutions.",
    "- SOX: internal controls over financial reporting for publicly traded companies.",
    "- COPPA: online collection of data from children under 13 requires parental consent.",
    "- FERPA: privacy of student education records.",
    "- Identity Theft and Assumption Deterrence Act, Digital Millennium Copyright Act (DMCA), CALEA, Economic Espionage Act (theft of trade secrets).",
    "- State laws: breach notification laws in all states; California CCPA/CPRA privacy rights.",
    "## International and European privacy",
    "The EU GDPR protects personal data of people in the EU and applies to any organization worldwide that processes it. Principles: lawfulness, fairness and transparency; purpose limitation; data minimization; accuracy; storage limitation; integrity and confidentiality; accountability. Rights: access, rectification, erasure (right to be forgotten), restriction, portability, objection. Roles: controller, processor, data subject, Data Protection Officer, supervisory authority. Breach notification to the supervisory authority within 72 hours; individuals without undue delay when high risk. Fines up to 4 percent of global turnover. Cross-border transfers need adequacy decisions or standard contractual clauses. Other laws: Canada PIPEDA, Brazil LGPD, China PIPL, Japan APPI.",
    "## PCI DSS",
    "The Payment Card Industry Data Security Standard is not a law. It is enforced contractually by the card brands through acquiring banks. It covers 12 requirements (network security, protect cardholder data, vulnerability management, access control, monitoring and testing, security policy). Tokenization and segmentation reduce scope.",
    "## Intellectual property",
    "- Copyright: protects original works of authorship (including code) automatically; lasts author's life plus 70 years (works for hire: 95 years from publication or 120 from creation).",
