    "- Motion detectors (infrared, heat-based, wave pattern, capacitance, photoelectric, passive audio), intrusion alarms (deterrent, repellent, notification; local or centralized), secondary verification (CCTV) to reduce false alarms.",
    "- CCTV is mainly detective (deterrent when visible); it requires monitoring or recording and retention.",
    "- Work areas: clean desk, screen privacy, visitor logs and escorts, secure areas by sensitivity.",
    "## Server rooms, data centers, wiring closets and media storage",
    "Restrict access (badges, biometrics, logging), avoid windows, use raised floors or overhead cabling, monitor environment and access. Wiring closets and intermediate distribution facilities must be locked. Media storage needs secure, climate-controlled rooms, inventory, and reuse sanitization. Evidence storage requires dedicated, logged, access-controlled storage to protect chain of custody.",
    "## Utilities and environment",
    "- Power: UPS (short-term power and line conditioning), generators (long-term), redundant feeds. Problems: fault (momentary loss), blackout (prolonged loss), sag (momentary low voltage), brownout (prolonged low voltage), spike (momentary high voltage), surge (prolonged high voltage), inrush (initial surge), noise (EMI and RFI interference), transients. Use surge protectors and line conditioners.",
    "- HVAC: temperature about 59-89.6 F (15-32 C, many target 64-81 F); humidity 40-60 percent (too low causes static, too high causes condensation and corrosion); positive pressurization keeps contaminants out.",
