    "- Fire classes (US): A common combustibles (water, soda acid), B flammable liquids (CO2, foam, halon substitutes), C electrical (CO2, halon substitutes; no water), D combustible metals (dry powder), K cooking oils (wet chemical).",
    "- Water systems: wet pipe (always full, fastest, risk of leaks/freezing), dry pipe (air until triggered, for cold areas), deluge (large volume, not for electronics), pre-action (dry until detection, then water released when sprinkler heads activate; best water-based option for data centers).",
