    "## Authorization mechanisms and principles",
    "- Implicit deny (deny by default), access control matrix (rows are subjects, columns objects), capability tables (per subject) versus access control lists (per object), constrained interfaces (menus, views, grayed-out options), content-dependent control (decision based on data content, such as database views) and context-dependent control (time, location, sequence of actions).",
    "- Need to know (access only to data required for the job), least privilege (only the permissions required), separation of duties (no single person completes a sensitive task alone), defense in depth.",
