    "- Rule-based access control: global rules apply to all subjects (firewall rules).",
    "- Attribute-Based Access Control (ABAC): policies use attributes of subject, object, action and environment (\"allow managers on company devices during business hours\"). Most granular; used in SDN and zero trust.",
    "- Mandatory Access Control (MAC): labels (classifications) on subjects and objects, enforced by the system; users cannot change them. Hierarchical, compartmentalized (need to know within compartments) and hybrid environments. Uses lattice-based model. Strongest and least flexible, used in military.",
    "- Risk-based access control: evaluates risk in real time (MFA step-up when risky, deny when very risky).",
